toaplan: save the scanline register's previous scanline in savestates

ToaScanlineRegister() sets its new-line bit by comparing the current scanline with the one it
returned last, kept in a function-local static that no savestate held. Games poll the
register until that bit is set, so after a load the 68000 spent a different number of cycles
in the poll than the run that saved the state did, depending on the scanline last read
before the load. Battle Garegga's mid-screen raster split then landed a line off (a desync
hundreds of frames after a load, with RAM still identical). The static becomes
nToaPreviousScanline, which ToaScanGP9001() saves (every caller is a GP9001 driver) and
ToaInitGP9001() clears.

Upstream: not merged yet; drop this file when the pinned commit contains the change
(docs/cores.md, "Patches").

